ANALYZE ran on the database (a `sqlite3` shell, a backup tool): it made
`sqlite_stat1`, which schema.sql never makes. SQLite's own tables are not
the schema's: it opens, with nothing to do.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE INDEX dish_name ON dish (name);
INSERT INTO dish (name) VALUES ('soup'), ('bread');
ANALYZE;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE INDEX dish_name ON dish (name);
